  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA-2000 and single profile (config_001) achieves 48.5% accuracy, far outperforming image-only ResNet50 (20.8%), establishing RNA as the dominant modality. Uncertainty: We have no information on whether aggregating multiple profiles (multiprofile) can improve on the single-profile RNA baseline. Question tested: config_002 isolates the effect of multiprofile + avgpool aggregation while keeping the same PCA-2000 encoder as the best baseline, making it a clean single-variable comparison to config_001. Why this is the best next experiment: With only 2 completed runs, the most efficient use of the next budget slot is to extend the strongest known direction (RNA) with the simplest new design axis (profile aggregation). If multiprofile+avgpool improves accuracy, it confirms aggregation is valuable and motivates testing transformer aggregation (config_003) next; if it does not, it tells us the single profile already captures the relevant signal and we should pivot to encoder improvements (scvi/scgpt). This experiment reduces the most critical uncertainty—whether profile aggregation matters—while building directly on the best evidence."
}

